                <pb facs="0544" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg410"/>

                <head>No. 278.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Walker to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-03-01"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 1, 1888</date>.
                        (Received April 6, 1888.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 92.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the 20th ultimo I addressed a note to
                    the Colombian minister of foreign affairs on the subject of quarantine
                    regulations at Panama, and on the 25th ultimo I received from him a reply, a
                    copy of which, with a translation, I have the honor to inclose herewith.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John G.
                        Walker</hi>.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d278-a1.xml" xpointer="d278-a1"/>
            </div>
